her": 423, "system": 31920, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 81643}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 233701}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "f4e7924f-f005-53dc-ab07-3535cd55d736", "at": 1795665497.2776194, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3062, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "58d01eaa-c2f0-5c8b-b5a2-6a66f378fd53", "at": 1795665499.488949, "until": 1795665500.5544956, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3063, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (36 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "751d7155-8ebd-53bd-97ef-f659c26cf61e", "at": 1795665500.5574272, "until": 1795665512.7197578, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3099, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01LC2BY6Y5VVUbuTaRhyBhWk", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && python3 - <<'EOF' import re s=open('Brief.md').read() a=s.index(\"- **Cross-dataset currency**\"); b=s.index(\"- **Noise yardstick**\") s=s[:a]+\"\"\"- …", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ns=open('Brief.md').read()\na=s.index(\"- **Cross-dataset currency**\"); b=s.index(\"- **Noise yardstick**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"- **Cross-dataset currency**: theory (BT, Fisher information; top-K identifiability theory of Chen et al. 2019) gives k\\\\* ≈ gap / (typical top influence) and SE ∝ 1/√N, so **k\\\\*/N ∝ z/√N** and k\\\\* ∝ z√N. Raw k\\\\*/N is therefore *not* comparable across datasets of different N. The study uses the **SE-unit fragility** F(C) = k\\\\*·g_max / SE(gap), g_max the largest per-comparison influence on the gap. In the linear regime the optimal k is the smallest k whose k largest influences sum to the gap, so k\\\\*·g_max ≥ gap, i.e. **F ≥ z and Q = F/z ≥ 1**, equal to 1 only if all influences equal g_max; Q's baseline depends on the shape of the influence distribution (light tail → near 1, heavy tail → larger) even for a perfectly specified BT model, and the exact nonlinear k\\\\* can lower it. So Q is read **only against its reference from the parametric-bootstrap null** (Q_real / Q_null on the same graph, counts and fitted scores), never as \"misfit\" on its own. Alternative if the synthetic check prefers it: replace g_max by the gap divided by the sum of the top-k influences, whose linear baseline is exactly 1 by construction. The quantity is named in the paper only after the synthetic-BT check. The SE entering F and z is the cluster-bootstrap SE (battle / question / game); the model-based Fisher SE is reported alongside, since their ratio is the clustering design effect. Raw k\\\\*/N is reported too, always next to the expected scaling and with equal-N subsampling.\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\na=s.index(\"- **Noise yardstick**\"); b=s.index(\"**Hypotheses\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"- **Noise yardstick**: the bootstrap/subsample flip probability P_flip(C) at the real N, and the **whole curve P_flip(f)** of random deletion at fraction f (approximately Φ(−z√(1−f))). Thresholds f_q (e.g. q = 5%, 16%) are used only where they lie inside (0, ~0.8): f_16% exists only for z > 1 and is beyond observation for large z, while for z < 1 P_flip already exceeds 16% at f = 0. The intent-vs-noise comparison (k\\\\*/N against f_q, and Q) is stated for a declared z-range, with no averaging across pairs outside it. Behaviour checked first on synthetic BT data (labelled synthetic).\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"- H4 (predictive rule): log k\\\\* ≈ a + b·log z + c·log √N + d·graph density (+ ties); fit on some datasets, tested out-of-sample on others; whether a design term improves held-out prediction is the operational form of \\\"does design matter\\\".\",\"- H4 (predictive rule): log k\\\\* ≈ a + b·log z + c·log √N + d·graph density (+ ties). The held-out unit is the dataset (leave-one-dataset-out, and leave-one-design-out), not the pair, since pairs of one graph are not independent; the number of effective held-out units is reported, and a \\\"design term improves held-out prediction\\\" result is limited to those instances. NBA seasons give many held-out units for the sports design only.\")\ns=s.replace(\"H1 (scaling): after SE-unit normalisation fragility collapses onto z across datasets (Q ≈ constant)\",\"H1 (scaling): after SE-unit normalisation fragility collapses onto z across datasets (F/z ≥ 1 with a common baseline given by the null)\")\ns=s.replace(\"differences between designs in Q (and in k\\\\*/(z√N)) beyond z and density are due to *misfit*, measured with the parametric-bootstrap null; if Real − Null ≈ 0\",\"differences between designs in Q (and in k\\\\*/(z√N)) beyond z and density are due to *misfit*, measured with the parametric-bootstrap null (Q_real vs Q_null); if Real − Null ≈ 0\")\ns=s.replace(\"(1) a common scale for noise and intent (SE-unit fragility, adversarial efficiency Q, P_flip)\",\"(1) a common scale for noise and intent (SE-unit fragility F, its ratio to the null, P_flip curves)\")\ns=s.replace(\"Q ≈ const and Real − Null ≈ 0\",\"F/z matches the null and Real − Null ≈ 0\")\nope\n[truncated for publication]"]], "output": "```console\n5b58cf3d697bc5c218f90d09cfd70b0941410c6d\tHEAD\nok\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "baec7b2d-68c8-5bbb-9f02-9974d8808cb1", "at": 1795665511.8291397, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3102, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "833c3458-b9f7-5b92-838b-0442d3141659", "at": 1795665511.831853, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3103, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "e13810b5-9868-5b76-95db-4874595dabbe", "at": 1795665511.834208, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3104, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "42c15971-6492-5753-9902-ff3e0379903d", "at": 1795665511.9498816, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3105, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "credential challenge GET /world/idea-re