layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "0965721d-94a0-53db-ab9c-de6453573889", "at": 1795665516.7756383, "until": 1795665516.9346356, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3121, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "e1d813f09325c73b0d16fc7b63a379e1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (61 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "I revised the Brief to revision 3, adopting all three corrections from the second review, and noted that in `idea-repo`#3. The wiki push succeeded.\n\n- **Q baseline:** Q = F/z is at least 1 in the linear regime, not equal to 1. It is read only against the parametric-bootstrap null (Q_real versus Q_null on the same graph, counts and fitted scores). The alternative of dividing the gap by the sum of the top-k influences stays as an option for the synthetic check. Q is named in the paper only after that check.\n- **Noise thresholds:** the Brief reports the whole P_flip(f) curve. The f_q thresholds are used only where they fall inside (0, ~0.8), and the intent-versus-noise comparison is stated for a declared z-range.\n- **H4 held-out unit:** it is the dataset or the design, not the pair. The paper reports the number of effective held-out units. NBA seasons give many units for the sports design only.\n- **Which SE:** the cluster-bootstrap SE enters F and z, and the model-based Fisher SE is reported alongside."}}, {"id": "ad486731-8a96-5ada-9d68-cac7b41b5e18", "at": 1795665516.9365814, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3183, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "se